; Supply-chain cooldown (ADR-211, decision 5): `npm install` / `npm update` only resolve versions
; published at least 7 days ago — direct AND transitive. Malicious versions are normally caught and
; unpublished well inside that window. `npm ci` installs the lockfile as-is and is not affected.
; A known vulnerability that reaches Yagra is the one exception: install the fix without waiting,
; e.g. `npm install <pkg>@<fixed> --min-release-age=0`, after checking its diff and
; `npm audit signatures`.
;
; Needs npm 11.10 or later. The npm 10 that ships with Node 22 (CI, web.Dockerfile) does not know
; the key and only warns about it — harmless there, because those only run `npm ci`.
min-release-age=7
